Go.dot patch 0002 for JUCE: a malformed WAV or AIFF file is refused, not read past its buffers.

JUCE's own fixes, in 8.0.17-security and 9.0.5, cherry-picked from JUCE's develop:
  62ee628181a5 "AIFF/WAV Audio Format: Fix a crash when reading files with
               malformed channel counts" (8c0c0d9b25ca on develop, Tom Poole, 2026-10-19)
  f8121f670878 "WAV and AIFF files: Harden metadata parsing"
               (8493b2c3caae on develop, Tom Poole, 2026-10-20)
Each develop commit applies cleanly to this pin (9.0.4+26, which they follow),
with Go.dot's notice after JUCE's licence block.

The faults: a channel count read from the file was sign-extended, so a header
saying 32768 channels or more made a reader with four billion of them, and a
frame wider than the reader's stack buffer read past it. Metadata chunks (WAV's
cue, LIST, smpl, inst, acid, bext, iXML, axml and the rest, AIFF's MARK, COMT,
INST) were read with lengths taken from the file, unchecked. Go.dot reads every sound it is given through
these readers - a drop onto the list, the media analyser, Tracktion's playback,
QLab and Ableton imports - so one damaged file could crash Go.dot as a show
loads. Now a reader is made only when the format holds together: a sample rate,
one channel or more, 8, 16, 24 or 32 bits, and a frame of channels x bits / 8.

What changes for Go.dot: a WAV or AIFF of another bit depth (12 or 20 bits, say,
which JUCE never decoded right) is now refused as not audio, where it used to be
opened and played wrong. A writer refuses a frame wider than 65535 bytes.

LINE ENDINGS. JUCE stores these files with CRLF in its own repository, so every
line of the hunks below ends in CRLF and must stay so; .gitattributes keeps this
file byte for byte (-text), and scripts/patches.py writes it as bytes.

Applied by Go.dot's build, cmake/WfgJucePatches.cmake, in the order
patches/JUCE/series gives; refreshed from the working tree with
scripts/patches.py JUCE refresh, which keeps this header. Against JUCE
7ff644f65d7d (9.0.4+26, the JUCE Tracktion Engine a5e44996f5f pins), where the
fixes are JUCE develop's own commits, cherry-picked. Drop it when the pin moves
to 9.0.5 or later. The author's decision of 2026-11-02.

